Shock  is caused by inadequate blood flow to the body’s organs. It can be caused by blood loss 
or loss of body fl uids, as may occur following untreated severe vomiting or diarrhea. Symptoms 
of shock may include the following:  
• Drowsiness  
• Confusion  
• Loss of consciousness  
• Extreme thirst  
• Pale skin color  
• Rapid heart rate  
• Cool, clammy skin  
• Rapid breathing  
• Anxiety
