In this situation, you should not remove the pressure bandage, even if blood seeps through it. Instead, reinforce the bandage around the original bandage to better control the bleeding. Continue applying pressure and monitor the victim for signs of shock. If necessary, elevate the victim's limb above their heart level to help reduce blood flow to the wound.
